 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Hard Boundaries:** Using labels restricts the method to hard boundaries between clusters. Fuzzy borders are not possible with this specific label-based implementation, though they could be implemented in GPU-based renderers [S1].
-*   **Hardware Limitations:** On hardware that only supports 1D transfer functions (like VolumePro1000), the volume must be pre-labeled. This limits flexibility but preserves interaction speed for hierarchy traversal since labeling is only needed once for initial clusters [S1].
